      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"MindWanderer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/48/4816_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MindWanderer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Oh, never mind–it is there, it just moved from an earlier version.</p>\n<p>Mention stuff here and a playtester will bring it up to GtG.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Which is precisely why I did what I did…</p>\n<p>Some thoughts on the “quantity of threat” given that a minion is half a lieutenant for most purposes, I expect it means minions are 1 and Lieutenants are 2, but it could be 1/2 and 1.</p>\n<p>I mean, it’s good enough as is I can houserule it into function, but not everyone is good with “buy-then-fix” rulebooks, and the previews are there specifically to catch these kinds of things.</p>",
